\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}

Recursive generation in base models imprints a differential depth response: central-tendency features drift with depth while shape features remain stable, enabling cross-generator depth classification (leak-free binary F1\,=\,0.694; end-to-end 3-class: 0.905) across eight generators from five families.
This decomposition establishes depth as an analytical axis for corpus provenance characterization, complementary to model-collapse analyses targeting retraining-induced degradation.
DDR suggests that fixed-parameter generation chains carry an inherent structural fingerprint; extending depth estimation to instruction-tuned and frontier-scale models remains the key open challenge.
